    "created_at": "2025-02-04T19:48:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-02-04T19:48:09Z",
    "body": "> Dialog doesn't fire toggle events (see [#9733](https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/9733)) but you can observe the `open` attribute and check `.matches(':modal')` to determine if it is now on the top layer.\n\nBeautiful! I just used this in one of my PlayWright tests:\n\n```js\n// Check if the dialog is in the top layer\nexpect(await page.locator('dialog[open]').evaluate(el => el.matches(':modal'))).toBe(true);\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
